> For the "Common Library Directory", how would I make sure it gets uploaded? Here is my deploy code:
> ```
> setwd("~/Dropbox/HMT/online")
> 
> rsconnect::setAccountInfo(name='openmodels',  token=..., secret=...)
> 
> library(rsconnect)
> deployApp(appTitle='PROSPER - UK Adapatation Support', appName='prosper')
> ```
**assistant**:
> To ensure the "Common Library Directory" (let’s call it `shared-code`) gets uploaded with your Shiny app when you deploy using `rsconnect::deployApp`, you’ll need to follow these steps:
> 
> ### Step 1: Directory Structure
> 
> Make sure your project directory is structured like this:
> 
> ```
> /online/
>     /shared-code/
>         shared_script.R
>     /shiny-app/
>         app.R
> ```
> 
> ### Step 2: Update Deployment Code
> 
> Modify the `deployApp` function to specify the app directory correctly while including the `shared-code` directory. You can set the `appFiles` parameter to include the shared code. Here’s how you might modify your deploy code:
> 
> ```r
> setwd("~/Dropbox/HMT/online")
> 
> rsconnect::setAccountInfo(name='openmodels',  token=..., secret=...)
> 
> library(rsconnect)
> 
> # Deploy with shared code
> deployApp(appTitle='PROSPER - UK Adaptation Support',
>           appName='prosper',
>           appDir = "shiny-app",  # Specify the app directory
>           appFiles = c("shared-code/shared_script.R",  # Include shared code
>                        "app.R"))  # Include necessary app files
> ```
> 
> ### Step 3: Update Sourcing in the App
> 
> Within your `app.R`, ensure you correctly source the shared script:
> 
> ```r
> source("shared-code/shared_script.R")
> ```
> 
> ### Step 4: Confirm Deployment
> 
> When you deploy the app, `rsconnect` will include the specified files in `appFiles`. After deployment, check the deployed app's file structure (if possible) to confirm that the `shared-code` directory and its contents are uploaded.
> 
> ### Step 5: Test the App
> 
> After deployment, test the app to confirm that it can access the shared code correctly. If you encounter issues, check the logs for errors and ensure that the paths used in `app.R` are correct.
> 
> ### Additional Note
> 
> If you find yourself adding multiple files or folders to `appFiles`, you can also consider using glob patterns to automatically include specific files or organize your main file structure to streamline this process.
